  SourceId: RXRnJcG4XSabZ35a
  Slug: bloodline-elemental
  DisplayName: 'Bloodline: Elemental'
  IconPath: icons/commodities/gems/pearl-brown-red.webp
  Description: "An elemental influence has imbued your blood with primal fury. You
    are granted different sorcerous gift spells and damage type from blood magic
    depending on which element affected your bloodline (see Elemental Influences
    below). Tradition primal Bloodline Skills Intimidation, Nature Sorcerous Gifts
    cantrip: see Elemental Influences below; 1st: see Elemental Influences below;
    2nd: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Resist Energy]; 3rd: see Elemental
    Influences below; 4th: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Unfettered Movement];
    5th: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Elemental Form] (elemental influence
    only); 6th :see Elemental Influences below; 7th: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Energy
    Aegis]; 8th: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Earthquake]; 9th: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Wrathful
    Storm] Bloodline Spells initial: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Elemental
    Toss]; advanced: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Elemental Motion]; greater:
    @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Elemental Blast] Blood Magic\u2014Elemental
    Fury Elemental energy wreathes your form and infuses your magic. Either you gain
    a +2 status bonus to Intimidation checks for 1 round, or a target takes 1 damage
    per spell rank; this damage type is listed under your elemental influence. If
    the spell already deals that type of damage, combine it with the spell's initial
    damage before determining weaknesses and resistances. Elemental Influences At
    1st level, choose the type of elemental that influenced your bloodline: air,
    earth, fire, metal, water, or wood. You can't change this later. You are granted
    different spells at certain ranks according to this influence. Air\u2014Sorcerous
    Gifts cantrip: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Gale Blast]; 1st: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Tailwind];
    3rd: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Wall of Wind]; 6th: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Chain
    Lightning]; Blood Magic Damage slashing Earth\u2014Sorcerous Gifts cantrip: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Scatter
    Scree]; 1st: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Pummeling Rubble]; 3rd: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Earthbind];
    6th: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Petrify]; Blood Magic Damage bludgeoning
    Fire\u2014Sorcerous Gifts cantrip: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Ignition],
    1st: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Breathe Fire]; 3rd: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Fireball];
    6th: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Tree of Seasons] (all pods are summer);
    Blood Magic Damage fire Metal\u2014Sorcerous Gifts cantrip @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Electric
    Arc]; 1st: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Thunderstrike]; 3rd: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Lightning
    Bolt]; 6th: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Chain Lightning]; Blood Magic
    Damage piercing Water\u2014Sorcerous Gifts cantrip: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Frostbite];
    1st: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Hydraulic Push]; 3rd: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Aqueous
    Orb]; 6th: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Scintillating Safeguard]; Blood
    Magic Damage bludgeoning Wood\u2014Sorcerous Gifts cantrip: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Tangle
    Vine]; 1st: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Cleanse Cuisine]; 3rd: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Wall
    of Thorns]; 6th: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Tangling Creepers]; Blood
    Magic Damage bludgeoning"
